{"version": 1, "branches": {"user": {"clock": 20, "levels": [[{"key": "turn3:assistant", "peer": "user", "value": "Yes \u2014 mute silences whispers and the aside for N turns without deleting anything.", "emb": null, "visibility": "private", "created": 20, "touched": 20, "mentions": [20], "history": [], "aliases": [], "refs": 0, "votes": 0, "strength": 1.0, "s_clock": 20}], [{"key": "turn2:assistant", "peer": "user", "value": "It keeps the center in view and confirms what matters between turns.", "emb": null, "visibility": "private", "created": 18, "touched": 18, "mentions": [18], "history": [], "aliases": [], "refs": 0, "votes": 0, "strength": 1.0, "s_clock": 18}, {"key": "turn3:user", "peer": "user", "value": "Can I quiet the memory block?", "emb": null, "visibility": "private", "created": 19, "touched": 19, "mentions": [19], "history": [], "aliases": [], "refs": 0, "votes": 0, "strength": 1.0, "s_clock": 19}], [{"key": "example-recall", "peer": "user", "value": "For recall demos: the sample dog's name is Biscuit, and the sample cat is named Marmalade.", "emb": null, "visibility": "private", "created": 13, "touched": 14, "mentions": [13, 14], "history": [], "aliases": [], "refs": 0, "votes": 0, "strength": 1.9885140203528962, "s_clock": 14}, {"key": "turn1:user", "peer": "user", "value": "How does the tree handle old memories?", "emb": null, "visibility": "private", "created": 15, "touched": 15, "mentions": [15], "history": [], "aliases": [], "refs": 0, "votes": 0, "strength": 1.0, "s_clock": 15}, {"key": "turn1:assistant", "peer": "user", "value": "They fade toward the roots and stay recallable \u2014 nothing is ever cut down.", "emb": null, "visibility": "private", "created": 16, "touched": 16, "mentions": [16], "history": [], "aliases": [], "refs": 0, "votes": 0, "strength": 1.0, "s_clock": 16}, {"key": "turn2:user", "peer": "user", "value": "What is the watchdog for?", "emb": null, "visibility": "private", "created": 17, "touched": 17, "mentions": [17], "history": [], "aliases": [], "refs": 0, "votes": 0, "strength": 1.0, "s_clock": 17}], [{"key": "project-north-star", "peer": "user", "value": "Continuity over novelty: a memory that survives a restart beats a cleverer one that doesn't.", "emb": null, "visibility": "private", "created": 1, "touched": 2, "mentions": [1, 2], "history": [], "aliases": [], "refs": 0, "votes": 0, "strength": 1.9885140203528962, "s_clock": 2}, {"key": "watchdog-role", "peer": "user", "value": "The watchdog tends the tree \u2014 keeps the center in view, confirms what matters, and never deletes; old memories fade toward the roots.", "emb": null, "visibility": "private", "created": 3, "touched": 4, "mentions": [3, 4], "history": [], "aliases": [], "refs": 0, "votes": 0, "strength": 1.9885140203528962, "s_clock": 4}, {"key": "whispers", "peer": "user", "value": "Whispers are the tree's associations: when something lands, nearby memories lean in on their own.", "emb": null, "visibility": "private", "created": 5, "touched": 6, "mentions": [5, 6], "history": [], "aliases": [], "refs": 0, "votes": 0, "strength": 1.9885140203528962, "s_clock": 6}, {"key": "recall-key", "peer": "user", "value": "Recall opens a whole memory from a few plain words. Exact keys hit at full confidence; free text is a search.", "emb": null, "visibility": "private", "created": 7, "touched": 8, "mentions": [7, 8], "history": [], "aliases": [], "refs": 0, "votes": 0, "strength": 1.9885140203528962, "s_clock": 8}, {"key": "mute", "peer": "user", "value": "Mute hushes the block without deleting anything. The tree keeps living; you just stop being interrupted.", "emb": null, "visibility": "private", "created": 9, "touched": 10, "mentions": [9, 10], "history": [], "aliases": [], "refs": 0, "votes": 0, "strength": 1.9885140203528962, "s_clock": 10}, {"key": "mailbox", "peer": "user", "value": "The mailbox keeps correspondence on its own branch so it never leaks into either side's memory block.", "emb": null, "visibility": "private", 